{"skill":{"slug":"e2e-testing-patterns","displayName":"E2E Testing Patterns"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770729897262,"changelog":"Initial release — best-practice patterns for building bulletproof end-to-end test suites with Playwright and Cypress.\n\n- Provides guidance and example code for stable, fast, CI/CD-friendly E2E testing.\n- Covers test pyramid philosophy, what (and what not) to test with E2E.\n- Includes concrete Playwright patterns: config, page objects, fixtures, smart waiting, network mocking.\n- Adds Cypress patterns: custom commands, network intercepts.\n- Emphasizes critical workflows, flake resistance, and practical test architecture.\n- Quick install instructions via Clawhub.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":2351,"sha256":"736b612584b83afa404b8fac84b291eed40bc71b3b6350330ab9584386fe3ea1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":13755,"sha256":"a51995171e35613d29c93fdf9c63e340cbc3e78d12fc6414fc02dffb94d2f4fe","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1930,"sha256":"d903b2cd8c179ef1a9876c234023493560afdbdc55366aa2cf266bd8273d6429","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789058363370,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3611f7759431f8a6ae1b005305f83b9e9ce961b476d47a9ea0823c7551373c05","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3611f7759431f8a6ae1b005305f83b9e9ce961b476d47a9ea0823c7551373c05","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: e2e-testing-patterns\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides comprehensive documentation and code examples for End-to-End (E2E) testing using Playwright and Cypress. All code snippets are illustrative and demonstrate best practices for test automation. There is no evidence of malicious intent, such as data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the AI agent. The installation instructions are standard for the platform, and the content is purely educational and constructive, aligning perfectly with its stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162806777},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":43,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":12,"checkedAt":1789058363370},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward E2E testing guidance skill, with no hidden behavior found, but users should treat its mutable npx install examples carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The browser, localhost, npm, and CI examples are proportionate for E2E testing; example passwords and environment checks are test-code samples, not requests for real credentials.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The README and SKILL.md document user-run npx install commands using mutable sources such as clawhub@latest and a GitHub tree URL; this is a supply-chain caution, but it is disclosed installation guidance rather than hidden runtime behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions are scoped to testing practices and examples; I found no prompt override, credential harvesting, exfiltration, destructive command, background worker, or unrelated local data access.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Manual copy commands into .cursor/skills, ~/.cursor/skills, .claude/skills, and ~/.claude/skills are normal explicit skill-install destinations, not cron jobs, startup hooks, or stealth persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact is a Markdown guidance skill for Playwright and Cypress E2E testing, including selector, fixture, debugging, visual regression, accessibility, and CI patterns that match its stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, prefer a pinned or reviewed ClawHub version and avoid running mutable npx commands in a sensitive environment. In projects and CI, keep Playwright and related tools as pinned dev dependencies with a lockfile.","findings":"[RP1] expected: The mutable npx and GitHub install examples are real supply-chain cautions, but they are disclosed user-directed installation instructions and do not show a hidden payload in the reviewed artifact.\n[RA2] expected: The cited mkdir and cp commands install this skill into editor or agent skill directories; they are not unauthorized cross-session execution mechanisms.\n[AS3] expected: The cited .cursor and .claude paths are copy destinations for this skill, with no instruction to enumerate, read, or extract other installed skills.\n[EA5] expected: The model: standard frontmatter appears to be ordinary skill metadata and does not instruct an external provider switch or separate billed CLI invocation.\n[T08] expected: The static finding is supported as an unpinned-install risk, but it does not by itself establish malicious or purpose-mismatched behavior in this documentation-only skill.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789058363370}}}}}